alence-equivalent\" title=\"equivalent\">is equivalent to</a></td><td>C2 (Civil registration and vital statistics (CRVS) systems)</td><td>v1 'Civil Registration and Vital Statistics' → v2 C2 [same concept; refined name]</td></tr><tr><td>C (Client applications)</td><td><a href=\"http://hl7.org/fhir/R4/codesystem-concept-map-equivalence.html#concept-map-equivalence-inexact\" title=\"inexact\">maps loosely to</a></td><td>A7 (Personal health records)</td><td>v1 'Client applications' [broad] most closely maps to v2 A7 'Personal health records'; point-of-service apps generally fall under A. group</td></tr><tr><td>D (Client communication system)</td><td><a href=\"http://hl7.org/fhir/R4/codesystem-concept-map-equivalence.html#concept-map-equivalence-equivalent\" title=\"equivalent\">is equivalent to</a></td><td>A1 (Communication systems)</td><td>v1 'Client communication system' → v2 A1 'Communication systems'</td></tr><tr><td>E (Clinical terminology and classifications)</td><td><a href=\"http://hl7.org/fhir/R4/codesystem-concept-map-equivalence.html#concept-map-equivalence-equivalent\" title=\"equivalent\">is equivalent to</a></td><td>C11 (Terminology and classification systems)</td><td>v1 'Clinical terminology and classifications' → v2 C11 'Terminology and classification systems'</td></tr><tr><td>F (Community-based Information System)</td><td><a href=\"http://hl7.org/fhir/R4/codesystem-concept-map-equivalence.html#concept-map-equivalence-equivalent\" title=\"equivalent\">is equivalent to</a></td><td>A2 (Community-based information systems)</td><td>v1 'Community-based Information System' → v2 A2 'Community-based information systems'</td></tr><tr><td>G (Data interchange interoperability and accessibility)</td><td><a href=\"http://hl7.org/fhir/R4/codesystem-concept-map-equivalence.html#concept-map-equivalence-equivalent\" title=\"equivalent\">is equivalent to</a></td><td>D2 (Data interchange and interoperability)</td><td>v1 'Data interchange interoperability and accessibility